  "title": "KYC page bank verification and Profile page bank details update the same data through different APIs",
  "description": "R6 deep audit finding. Dimension: wiring. Severity: P2. Source SHA: bbd487a3. Scope: R6_DEEP_AUDIT_WAVE. The KYC page has a Bank Verification tab that calls `verifyBankAccount()` (api.ts line 853) which hits `/api/v1/supplier/kyc/verify-bank`. The Profile page Bank Details tab calls `updateSupplierProfile({ bankDetails: ... })` which hits a different endpoint. Both update the supplier's bank information, but through completely separate API paths with different validation rules. The KYC bank flow includes IFSC lookup validation and sets bankVerificationStatus, while the Profile flow just saves raw data. A user could save bank details in Profile bypassing the KYC verification flow entirely.",
